## 🔄 Test Generation Workflow Rules

### **[Main Generation Orchestrator](mdc:MainGenerationOrchestrator.mdc)**
- **ID**: `main_generation_orchestrator`
- **Purpose**: Drives complete test generation workflow through all phases
- **Scope**: End-to-end test generation process
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Phase sequence enforcement
  - 100% research completion verification
  - Phase gate controls (no skipping allowed)
  - Architecture overview
  - Success criteria

### **[Phase 0: Reusability Analysis](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_0_reusability`
- **Purpose**: Test analysis, component reusability check, modification protocol
- **Scope**: Initial test analysis phase
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Test description analysis
  - Existing component discovery (Page Objects, Business, Locators)
  - Reusability vs new creation decisions
  - Safe extension/modification protocol
  - Backward compatibility requirements

### **[Phase 1: Locator Research](mdc:Phase1_LocatorResearch.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_1_locator_research`
- **Purpose**: Page investigation, element collection, locator generation
- **Scope**: NEW components only (reusable components skip this phase)
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Page state capture (Playwright snapshots)
  - Element HTML collection (`browser_evaluate`)
  - Locator generation from real data
  - Playwright best practices (text-based → placeholder → attributes → role → ID → class)
  - Investigation sequence documentation

### **[Phase 2: Pre-Generation Verification](mdc:Phase2_PreGenerationVerification.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_2_verification`
- **Purpose**: 100% research completion gate before code generation
- **Scope**: Research completion checkpoint
- **Status**: Active - CRITICAL GATE
- **Key Topics**:
  - Research completion verification (100% required)
  - Cross-reference test steps with investigation findings
  - NEW components vs EXISTING components coverage
  - Research Completion Checklist
  - Prohibition enforcement (no code generation if incomplete)
  - Complexity-based research continuation protocol

### **[Phase 3: Implementation Standards](mdc:Phase3_ImplementationStandards.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_3_implementation`
- **Purpose**: Implementation patterns, verification requirements, best practices
- **Scope**: Code implementation phase
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Base class usage (AIPage, AIElement)
  - Hierarchical logging (TestLogger integration)
  - Table view detection (AITomsPage compatibility)
  - Cache-first approach
  - Page load verification (domcontentloaded)
  - Element availability verification (waitFor)
  - Action completion verification
  - Navigation retry logic
  - Complex generation checkpoint management

### **[Phase 4: Test Generation](mdc:Phase4_TestGeneration.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_4_test_generation`
- **Purpose**: Final test code generation standards and requirements
- **Scope**: Test code generation (blocked until Phase 2 passes)
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - One test per file mandate
  - Complete test coverage (100% of test description)
  - Test scenario structure with tagging
  - Layered architecture enforcement (Test → Business → Page Objects → AIElement)
  - SettingsHelper usage (no hardcoded URLs/credentials)
  - TagHelper.taggedTest() integration
  - Hierarchical logging integration

### **[Phase 5: Validation](mdc:Phase5_Validation.mdc)**
- **ID**: `phase_5_validation`
- **Purpose**: Test execution, regression testing, 100% pass rate verification
- **Scope**: Test validation and execution
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Regression testing (if classes modified)
  - New test execution parameters (`--workers=1 --headed --project=chromium`)
  - 100% pass rate mandate
  - Project structure compliance verification
  - Regeneration until success

