## 🏗️ Architecture & Pattern Rules

### **[Layered Architecture](mdc:ArchitectureLayeredDesign.mdc)**
- **ID**: `architecture_layered`
- **Purpose**: Defines layered architecture requirements and restrictions
- **Scope**: All test automation code
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Layer responsibilities (Test Scenario → Business → Page Objects → AIElement → Cache)
  - Direct locator prohibition (ONLY AIElement accesses locators)
  - No direct Playwright API usage in high-level layers
  - Proper call hierarchy enforcement
  - Single responsibility per layer

### **[Locator Management](mdc:LocatorManagementSystem.mdc)**
- **ID**: `locator_management`
- **Purpose**: Locator cache structure, generation rules, AIElement integration
- **Scope**: Locator handling across all layers
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Cache location (`tests/Utils/locator_cache.json`)
  - Cache structure (PageName → locators → elementKey)
  - Priority order (Cache first → AI fallback → Error)
  - Element HTML collection workflow
  - Locator generation rules (Playwright best practices)
  - AIElement cache lookup mechanism

### **[Tagging Standards](mdc:TaggingStandards.mdc)**
- **ID**: `tagging_standards`
- **Purpose**: Test tagging requirements, categories, and generation rules
- **Scope**: Test tagging and execution filtering
- **Status**: Active
- **Key Topics**:
  - Tag categories (suite, priority, type, dataImpact, environment, stability, speed, feature, component, team)
  - TestId format (`TC_XXX_vYYY_DescriptiveName`)
  - TestTagsMapping.json structure
  - TagConfiguration.json for validation
  - TagHelper.taggedTest() wrapper requirement
  - Extensible tag reuse rules
  - No manual tag annotations allowed

### **Hierarchical Logging Standards**
- **Purpose**: TestLogger usage standards across all layers
- **Scope**: All test automation code
- **Status**: Integrated into phase rules
- **Key Topics**:
  - TestLogger methods per layer (testStep, businessStep, pageStep, elementStep)
  - Human-readable descriptions requirement
  - NO console.log usage
  - Complete coverage (ALL public methods wrapped)
- **See**: **[Phase3_ImplementationStandards](mdc:Phase3_ImplementationStandards.mdc)**, **[Phase4_TestGeneration](mdc:Phase4_TestGeneration.mdc)**

